      "supported": true,
      "coverage": "full",
      "coverage_explanation": "Exercises initial OFF, falling-edge start/stop, sustained presses, release immunity, repeated blinking, stopping while illuminated, and restart with a fresh timer. Successive blinking intervals are checked against 500±20ms. First-edge windows allow both the 20ms input-recognition delay and the toggle tolerance; later absolute windows expand cumulatively rather than imposing a fixed phase error.",
      "assumptions": [
        "Relies on the disclosed bench defaults: the D13 LED is active HIGH to GND, and the D2 button connects to GND.",
        "D2 INPUT_PULLUP and active-LOW pressing are explicitly required.",
        "Inputs are stable and bounce-free; no particular debounce implementation is required.",
        "The first toggle may occur 480..540ms after a start input, allowing up to 20ms input recognition plus a 500±20ms timer interval. Each subsequent interval independently permits 480..520ms.",
        "Edge-free state windows begin after the latest permitted boundary transition. No application parameters are missing."
